                                            <InArgument x:TypeArguments="x:String" xml:space="preserve">["&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt; &lt;html lang=""en""&gt; &lt;head&gt; &lt;meta charset=""UTF-8""&gt; &lt;body style=""font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #000;""&gt; &lt;p&gt;Thank you for your request.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Please find attached a blank document. Once completed, please return to us by attaching it in a reply to this email &lt;span style=""color: #d4351c;""&gt;and amending the subject line to Completed Catch Certificate.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Once we receive your completed document it will be validated and returned to you by email. Please ensure the document is completed fully or we will not be able to validate it. As the Fish Exports Service is currently unavailable, documents will not transfer automatically to EU Catch. Once validated, please share the document directly with your importer. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;table border=""1"" cellpadding=""8"" cellspacing=""0"" style=""border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #000;""&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; You may be liable to investigation and enforcement action, including prosecution, if you knowingly submit false, misleading, or otherwise inaccurate data. &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt;By submitting this catch certificate, you confirm that:&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul style=""margin-top: 0;""&gt; &lt;li&gt;you understand that you are under a duty not to knowingly submit information that is false or otherwise inaccurate&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;the fisheries administrations may undertake checks on the accuracy and validity of the data, cross-reference it with data held and submitted by others in the supply chain, and exchange data with other relevant fisheries administrations, including those in the country of export&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;you understand that you may be liable to investigation and potentially to enforcement action, including prosecution, if you knowingly submit false, misleading, or otherwise inaccurate data&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; For guidance on fish species please see: &lt;a href=""http://www.fao.org/fishery/collection/asfis/en""&gt; http://www.fao.org/fishery/collection/asfis/en &lt;/a&gt;. To see a list of licensed fishing vessels please see: &lt;a href=""https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/uk-vessel-lists""&gt; https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/uk-vessel-lists &lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;The mandatory fields you must complete are as follows:&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Section 2: fishing vessel name, call sign/PLN, fishing licence number, fishing gear&lt;br&gt; Section 3: species, product code, catch area(s), net catch weight in kg&lt;br&gt; Section 5: Name and signature of the master of the vessel&lt;br&gt; Section 8: Name of exporter and date of acceptance&lt;br&gt; Annex 1: exporter name and address &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Use &lt;a href=""https://www.gov.uk/guidance/temporary-fish-exports-guidance""&gt; https://www.gov.uk/guidance/temporary-fish-exports-guidance &lt;/a&gt; for additional information. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;/body&gt; &lt;/html&gt;"]</InArgument>
